# BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore file (#428): every build of backend/Dockerfile uses the repository
# root as its context (image.yml, compose.yml, `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`), so these
# patterns are relative to the root, not to backend/. The old backend/.dockerignore never applied:
# Docker reads .dockerignore only from the root of the context.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
backend/servers.json
.git
.claude
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.dump
**/*.age
**/*.key
